{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Designated to a man.</b> Designated and set aside for a man — and I do not know a parallel for it in Scripture. And it speaks of a Canaanite maidservant, half slave and half free, betrothed to a Hebrew slave who is permitted in a maidservant." "<b>And her redemption has not been effected.</b> Redeemed and not redeemed; and an unspecified redemption is by money." "<b>Or freed.</b> By a deed of manumission (Sifra)." "<b>There shall be an inquiry.</b> She is lashed and not he; it is upon the court to investigate the matter so as not to obligate her the death penalty <b>for she has not been freed</b> — and her betrothal is not full betrothal. And our Rabbis learned from here (Makkot 22) that one who is in lashes — there is a reading, that the judges who administer the lashes read over the one being lashed: ״If you do not take care to do…״ and ״HaShem will strike you with extraordinary plagues…״ (Deuteronomy 28)." "<b>For she has not been freed.</b> Therefore he is not liable the death penalty for her, for her betrothal is not betrothal; but if she was freed, her betrothal is betrothal and he is liable the death penalty (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:12.813466257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}